course: dictionary
lesson: 12725
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and dragging is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits. «He was dragging the heavy box up the stairs» means pulling it with effort, because heavy and up the stairs are the clues.
explain: Read the whole sentence, then ask which meaning fits. «The afternoon was dragging on and on» is not about pulling anything. A day that drags feels slow and boring, so the time is passing very slowly.
explain: On a computer, «Drag the picture into the folder» means hold the mouse button and slide the picture. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Dragging is the -ing form of drag: drag, drags, dragged, dragging.
fact: «Dragging» can mean pulling something heavy along the ground with effort.
fact: «Dragging» can mean moving something on a screen by holding the mouse button or your finger on it and sliding it.
fact: «Dragging» can mean making someone go somewhere they don't want to go, or letting something trail along the ground.
fact: «Drag and drop» means moving a file or picture on a computer by dragging it and then letting go.
exercise: «He was dragging the heavy box up the stairs.» What is dragging here? | *Pulling something heavy along with effort | Lifting something light into the air | Singing loudly | Painting the stairs
exercise: «The lesson was dragging, and I kept checking the clock.» What does dragging mean? | Pulling a sledge | *Going on slowly and boringly | Holding a mouse button | Running very fast
exercise: To move a file on a computer, you can use «drag and drop». What does it mean? | Print the file | Delete the file at once | Open the file in a new window | *Hold the mouse button, slide the file, and let go
test: «Her dog was dragging its lead along the path.» What is dragging here? | Carrying a bag on her back | *Letting something trail along the ground | Jumping over a puddle | Barking at a cat
test: «Dad is dragging the twins to the shop, though they do not want to go.» What does dragging mean? | Lifting the shopping bags | Running ahead of everyone | *Making someone go somewhere they do not want to go | Shouting at the shop
exam: In science, dragging a heavy box across the floor shows which force? | Sound | Gravity | *Friction | Magnetism
